Package: killall
Version: 22.21-r0
Description: Utilities for managing processes on your system
 The psmisc package contains utilities for managing processes on your
 system: pstree, killall and fuser.  The pstree command displays a tree
 structure of all of the running processes on your system.  The killall
 command sends a specified signal (SIGTERM if nothing is specified) to
 processes identified by name.  The fuser command identifies the PIDs of
 processes that are using specified files or filesystems.
Section: base
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Poky <poky@yoctoproject.org>
License: GPLv2
Architecture: cortexa9-vfp-neon
OE: psmisc
Depends: update-alternatives-opkg, libc6 (>= 2.21)
Source: http://downloads.sourceforge.net/psmisc/psmisc-22.21.tar.gz file://0001-Typo-in-fuser-makes-M-on-all-the-time.patch file://0002-Include-limits.h-for-PATH_MAX.patch
